course: dictionary
lesson: 6743
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «once» can mean different things, and the words around it show you which meaning to use. «Once there was a king» starts a story, so once means a time long ago. «Once you finish, you can play» tells you when you can play: as soon as you finish.
explain: Some phrases with once have their own meanings. «At once» means right now. «All at once» means together or suddenly. «Once in a blue moon» means very rarely, so it is not about the moon at all.
explain: Casual talk uses once in its own ways. «For once» means this time, unlike usual, and often sounds like a complaint: «Be on time for once!» In parts of the UK and Ireland, «the once» means one time only: «I only did it the once.»
fact: Once can mean one time, as in «Lightning can strike the same place more than once».
fact: Once can mean at some time in the past, as in «Once upon a time» at the start of a fairy tale.
fact: Once can mean as soon as, as in «Once the water boils» in a science experiment.
fact: «At once» means now, right away, or at the same time.
fact: «Once and for all» means for good, so that the problem is settled and will not come back.
exercise: «Once upon a time there lived a dragon.» What does once mean here? | *At some time in the past | As soon as | Right now | One time only
exercise: «Once you finish your tea, you can go out.» What does once mean here? | At the same time | Only one time | For once | *As soon as
exercise: Mum says, «Tidy your room at once!» What does at once mean? | Sometime next year | *Now, right away | Only one time | Very rarely
test: «Be quiet for once!» Mum sighs. What does for once mean here? | At the same time | Only one time ever | Forever | *This time, unlike usual, with a complaint
test: «I only did it the once.» What does the once mean? | Many times | *One time only | Never | Every day
exam: «Lightning can strike the same place more than once.» What does more than once mean? | Never again | *Many times | Only at night | Very quickly
